# .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# Scoped narrowly to CI/CD workflow definitions, not the whole repo —
# this repo otherwise welcomes outside contributions per the
# civic-standards:openness posture. The one thing that needs an explicit
# human gate is anything that runs unattended with repo secrets
# (LIMS_API_KEY, LEGISTAR_TOKEN_*, OPEN_STATES_API_KEY) on a schedule —
# see .github/workflows/refresh-meetings.yml's own header for exactly
# that risk (a merged edit to a workflow file executes with those
# secrets available on its next scheduled run, unlike a pull_request-
# triggered run, which never gets secrets injected at all).
#
# Paired with branch protection on main ("Require review from Code
# Owners"), this means any PR touching a workflow file needs @ngabantudev
# to explicitly approve it before it can merge — a fork or an outside
# contributor can open a PR that edits these files, but it can't land
# without that sign-off. Includes this file itself, so ownership can't be
# quietly stripped by the same kind of PR it's meant to gate.

/.github/workflows/ @ngabantudev
/.github/CODEOWNERS @ngabantudev
